@__alpoge__ shares a story about the Jacobian conjecture, a famous open problem in mathematics, which he claims is false. He describes a specific polynomial map from igure 3 to igure 3 with a Jacobian determinant of -2, and details points it maps to and from, illustrating the complexity involved in such problems.

The linked articles discuss the future of mathematics and AI, including Julia Kempe's views on why math may fall next and the potential for superhuman provers, as well as Christian Szegedy's insights on building frontier labs and his shift from xAI to formal mathematics research.

